      },
      "object 27": {
        "ID": 27,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "310.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. Click the button again and again and watch the state below prob: 0 is mostly followed by 1, and 2 always by 0. Click dump: every transition comes out of the right outlet, and the box shows the last one, 2 0 1.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 28": {
        "ID": 28,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "440.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "3. Add a transition: type 4 into the right box, 2 into the middle and then 0 into the left one, which sends 0 2 4. A pair already stored gets the new weight, so from 0 it is now 3 to 4 for state 2. A weight of 0 switches a transition off.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 29": {
        "ID": 29,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "590.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "4. Click 3: a number sets the state without sending anything. State 3 has no way out, so the next bang sends nothing and bangs the middle outlet, counted below it. The chain goes back to state 0, its first argument, and the bang after that goes on from there.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
